--- body ---
## Context

Ticket 0345 collapsed the slides writing build to consume committed handoff
artifacts only, and 0352 did the same for the report side. The 0352 celebrate
sweep used `make -B -n` (force-rebuild dry-run) as the strict clean-room test
and found the slides side still fails:

- `make -n slides` — 0 `uv run` (passes — but only because timestamps happen
  to be fresh)
- `make -B -n slides` — **42 `uv run` lines**

Root cause: the `slides/slides.pdf` rule in the root Makefile lists prereqs
whose recipes are still in the root Makefile (`fig_direct_p1_base.pdf`,
`fig_capability_timeline.pdf`, `fig_spider_cross_exp.pdf`,
`fig_method_convergence.pdf` via SLIDE_GEN, `fig_regimes_scatter.pdf`,
`fig_scaling_curve.pdf`, `macros_p1_base.tex` grouped with the p1_base figure,
and the SLIDE_GEN cp-from-report rules). These rules survived 0345 — that
ticket fixed the Exp2-specific producer duplication, not the broader
workpackage split for slides.

0352 added `tests/test_report_build_clean_room.py` which guards report under
both `-n` and `-B -n`. The analogous slides test should ship alongside the
fix here (or via 0353, which is now unblocked and explicitly scoped to the
class regression guard).

## Relevant files
- `Makefile` — `slides/slides.pdf` rule (~line 155 post-0352) and its
  uv-run prereq rules (fig_direct_p1_base, fig_capability_timeline,
  fig_spider_cross_exp, fig_method_convergence, fig_regimes_scatter,
  fig_scaling_curve, macros_p1_base, SLIDE_GEN copies)
- `experiments/analysis.mk` — destination for migrated rules; already has
  `exp1-analysis-figures` and the new `report-figures` phony from 0352
- `slides/Makefile` — already clean (just runs tectonic)
- `tests/test_report_build_clean_room.py` — pattern for the slides
  equivalent
- `.claude/rules/coding-python.md` — Build section, workpackage-split rule

## Actions
1. Inventory every prerequisite of `slides/slides.pdf` in the root
   Makefile. Classify: (a) committed handoff artifact with no recipe, or
   (b) `uv run` analysis rule.
2. For each (b): move the rule into `experiments/analysis.mk` under a new
   `slides-figures` phony (mirror of 0352's `report-tables`). Confirm the
   target artifact is already committed; do not bundle regeneration.
3. Audit the SLIDE_GEN `cp` rules (`$(SLIDE_GEN)/regimes.csv: $(GEN)/regimes.csv`
   etc.) — these are simple copies, fine if both sides are committed, but
   the producer must live in analysis.mk.
4. The `figures:` alias in root Makefile becomes fully delegatable, mirroring
   what 0352 did for `tables:`.

## Test
`make -B -n slides` must contain zero `uv run` invocations. Same test pattern
as `tests/test_report_build_clean_room.py`. If 0353 has already shipped a
class-level test by the time this ticket runs, that test will fail until
this work is done — that's the desired ordering.

## Verification
- [ ] `make -n slides` shows no `uv run`
- [ ] `make -B -n slides` (force rebuild) shows no `uv run`
- [ ] All `slides/slides.pdf` prerequisites are committed
      (`git cat-file -e HEAD:<path>`)
- [ ] Slides-side analysis rules now live in `experiments/analysis.mk`
- [ ] `make check` passes

## Invariants
- Do not break `make report` (0352's clean-room property must hold)
- Producer code and CLI arguments must not change — recipe-location-only
  migration (per 0352's updated Invariants language)
- Slides PDFs remain visually equivalent after regeneration

## Exit criteria
- `make slides` (writing build) contains no `uv run` / data-access rules
  under either plain `-n` or `-B -n` — compiles from committed handoff
  artifacts only
- `experiments/analysis.mk` is the sole producer of slides figures
- Companion adherence test (here or via 0353) guards the invariant
- `make check` passes
